INSERT INTO `SERVMASK_PREFIX_comments` VALUES (1464,1232,'Emmapn','hixs79@mail220v.org','https://seasonal-palette.top','178.20.208.181','2026-09-21 17:01:52','2026-09-21 23:01:52','I am planning a capsule wardrobe and want to confirm my season before choosing the main colors. A few simple assessments indicate autumn although the exact subtype changes. Soft brown and moss are dependable but mustard and strong rust can make my complexion look uneven. Since I am keeping the wardrobe compact each neutral and accent needs to combine easily with the others. [url=https://seasonal-palette.top]autumn seasonal palette[/url] gives me a starting list to compare but I would like to validate the direction with actual fabric. The initial test could include cream, warm navy, chocolate, olive, muted teal, and brick. I can make consistently exposed photos in indirect daylight using the same camera settings. For the neutrals should I focus more on skin clarity or on harmony with my hair and eyes? I need two useful accent shades that can work across casual and slightly formal outfits. Muted teal seems promising while brick red may be easier than orange. Does this set separate autumn clearly or should I add a cooler control color for comparison? A short practical test list would help me avoid buying colors based only on a label. The main goal is practical coordination rather than following every suggested autumn shade. I would value examples from similar palettes',0,'0','Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 10.0; Win64; x64) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/130.0.0.0 Safari/537.36','comment',0,0);
